WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.810
The third planet in the Tau Ceti system,

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.360
Sea of the Morningstar.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.810
As with most newly settled planets,

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.650
once generations passed and its population increased,

00:00:08.650 --> 00:00:10.150
relations with its overseer, the Stellar Alliance, worsened.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.070
And a war of independence began.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:13.280
To complement their meager fleet,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.160
the government of Sea of the Morningstar

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:17.370
issued Letters of Marque.

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.120
And legal space pirates were born.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.000
Over a hundred years have passed since the war's end,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.880
and this is a story of pirates sailing the seas of space.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.340
It's time for some piracy!

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:09.560
I am the captain of this ship.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.150
Who are you?

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:14.530
You're lying.

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:18.110
The captain of the Bentenmaru is a man.

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:19.700
I know that much.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.530
Get me Captain Kato.

00:02:24.790 --> 00:02:28.870
The Bentenmaru's captain passed away...

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:30.880
Did you know the previous captain?

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.290
I'm the captain now.

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.460
You're lying!

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:34.920
Gonzaemon's...

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.300
No one told me that Captain Kato was dead!

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.630
Stop these terrible lies!

00:02:39.050 --> 00:02:42.470
Information on the pirate captains with Letters of Marque

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.720
is available on the public net.

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.100
I'm not lying.

00:02:46.930 --> 00:02:48.640
Who are you?

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.940
Kato Marika,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:51.850
his daughter.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:59.360
Coorie, send her the data about the Bentenmaru having a new captain.

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.240
Roger.

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:05.200
The captain of the space pirate ship, the Bentenmaru,
perished in an unfortunate accident.
The Bentenmaru's pirating license
is currently in a grace period.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.830
I'm sorry I accused you of lying.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.550
It never occurred to me that he might have passed away.

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:20.010
I am Princess Gruier Serenity.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.680
Seventh princess of the Serenity royal family.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:30.730
Who's that?

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:33.310
A great royal family.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.270
They aren't as old as the Galactic Empire's kings,

00:03:36.270 --> 00:03:40.490
but reliable family trees can trace their lineage back over a hundred generations.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:43.360
Why would someone like that stow away on our ship?

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:47.120
Does anyone here have current information on the Serenity royal family?

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.370
I've only seen stuff about them in the headlines.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.830
They have nothing to do with us.

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.090
Get the information quickly.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.460
Keep talking to her, Captain.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:58.960
Right!

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.220
Sorry to keep you waiting, Princess Gruier Serenity.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.970
I'm Kato Marika, Captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:10.310
It's strange, isn't it?

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.520
Repeating our names like this...

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.980
Please call me Marika.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.940
You may call me Gruier.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.490
Um...

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:25.360
If it would be all right, would you remove whatever is blocking the camera,

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.950
so we can see your face?

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:32.580
You can see me, so we'd be even...

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.630
Is that not okay?

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:37.290
Thought so.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.050
It is a pleasure to meet you, Marika.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.390
I am Gruier.

00:04:48.140 --> 00:04:52.350
I apologize for boarding without the captain's permission.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.640
Would you extend permission to me?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.650
Yes... You have permission.

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.400
Welcome to the Bentenmaru.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.690
Thank you, Captain.

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.240
She's the real thing.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.320
Princess Gruier Serenity...

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.700
Her data matches what is provided by the royal family.

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:14.790
So it really is her...

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:19.670
All right, Gruier.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.760
I'm going to send someone to guide you around the ship.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.340
Let's see...

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.010
Schnitzer.

00:05:26.010 --> 00:05:30.140
Head to the docking control room, and give her an escort.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:31.850
Me?

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:34.270
You want me to escort her around the ship?

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:36.480
Sure that's a good idea with someone who hasn't seen me before?

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:40.650
She might be a little surprised, but it'll be okay.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:41.980
I was fine.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.190
No. I refuse.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.740
Oh, all right...

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.120
Then, Kane.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:52.740
Wh-Where am I escorting her, anyway?

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:55.200
We don't have any luxury rooms here!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.790
Oh, yeah...

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.210
Well, she can't go to the captain's quarters...

00:05:59.210 --> 00:06:02.040
And the cafeteria is definitely not an option!

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:05.210
Misa, is there anywhere on board that she can go?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.630
Let me think...

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.220
Maybe the room where we keep those we've kidnapped?

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.220
The optional room.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.640
What? There? Isn't there anywhere else she can stay?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.650
I am Gruier Serenity.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.490
I apologize again for stowing away on your ship.

00:06:27.490 --> 00:06:29.610
Please allow me aboard the Bentenmaru.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.080
Oh... Well, I'm the captain, Marika.

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:41.000
Welcome aboard the Bentenmaru, Princess...

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.960
Wait, no... It's Gruier, right?

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:46.010
You are welcome here.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.050
Thank you, Captain.

00:06:50.050 --> 00:06:52.970
I suppose I'll have to get accustomed to it...

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:55.390
Your face is very similar to your father's.

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:58.020
Is it?

00:06:58.020 --> 00:07:00.310
I never met my father.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.850
What kind of person was he?

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.320
He was wonderful.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:06.690
Hey, hey.

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.280
I apologize for my rudeness earlier.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.200
I didn't know he had passed away...

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:14.330
Don't worry about it.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.330
Geez, I'm not good at this.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:17.450
Oh, right.

00:07:17.450 --> 00:07:19.000
I'll introduce my crew.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.460
Please do!

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:25.130
First, the man who brought you here is our helmsman,

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:26.840
Kane McDougal.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:29.220
It was an honor.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:31.050
Right, right.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:31.630
Next...

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:33.970
Misa Grandwood, the ship physician.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.510
You appear to be under a lot of stress.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:37.520
You're too thin.

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.730
I get that a lot.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:42.520
Coorie, our electronic warfare specialist.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:45.400
Sorry that I'm still seated.

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:46.360
It's fine!

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:49.190
Our tactical officer, Schnitzer.

00:07:49.190 --> 00:07:50.110
He's a cyborg.

00:07:51.570 --> 00:07:52.950
How wonderful!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.200
Our navigator, Luca.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:58.240
I can see it...

00:07:58.240 --> 00:08:00.500
No, we don't need you to see anything right now.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.750
Hyakume, our radar and sensor specialist.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.880
Hi there, Princess.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:07.380
San-Daime is in charge of our engines.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:08.210
Hi.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.170
And I'm Kato Marika, the trainee captain.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:16.540
Captain, don't call yourself a trainee when we have guests—

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:17.430
No.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:20.220
She's an important guest,

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:22.230
so I don't think we should be hiding things.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:25.100
She'd find out quickly, anyway.

00:08:25.100 --> 00:08:26.110
Right, right.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:29.690
These are the Bentenmaru's primary crew members.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:31.820
Whenever there's an important decision to make,

00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:34.240
I usually talk to them.

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.780
Don't worry...

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.620
They're all first-rate pirates who worked under my father.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:48.420
I have come here with a request for you space pirates,

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:50.500
you who bear a Letter of Marque.

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.050
A request?

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:54.010
What is it?

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.990
It's about...

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.350
A ghost ship.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.220
I'd like you to find the wandering golden ghost ship.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.060
The golden ghost ship?

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:09.070
Sorry to interrupt...

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.150
Seventh Princess of the Serenity System, Princess Gruier Serenity Missing

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.440
"The Serenity Royal Government has just announced

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.820
that Princess Gruier Serenity is missing.
Seventh Princess of the Serenity System, Princess Gruier Serenity Missing

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:18.820
An investigation is underway to determine her whereabouts,

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:20.490
and whether she was the victim of foul play.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:23.790
No... I'm here of my own will!

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:27.750
Misa, where did this job come from?

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:30.710
From the Harold Lloyd Insurance Union, like always.

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:33.710
And where are the escort ships guarding the Symphony Angel from?

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.430
The Serenity Stellar Defense Forces.

00:09:36.430 --> 00:09:38.840
Three escort ships isn't that many,

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.180
and I guess they were to protect the princess.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:47.940
Contact Shou at the Insurance Union.

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.310
I want to know more about this.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.400
What do we do about the princess?

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.570
If they ask, answer honestly.

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.780
If not, don't say anything.

00:09:55.780 --> 00:09:58.360
I'm not getting executed for treason against the royal family.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.410
You don't need to worry about that.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.870
I'm here on this ship

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.790
of my own will...

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.460
Treason? Never...

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:11.670
Don't worry.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:13.090
We won't hurt you.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.800
Princess Gruier.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.470
As captain of the Bentenmaru, I accept your task.

00:10:22.760 --> 00:10:23.760
Leave it to us.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:46.870
S-So, I'd like to introduce you all to your new friend...

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.790
I am the seventh princess of the Serenity royal family.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:52.750
Gruier Serenity.

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:55.590
It's a pleasure to meet you all.

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.300
Marika!

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.680
Did you see the princess in the middle school?

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:07.730
Um...

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.560
I guess.

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.770
If you haven't already, you should!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:15.820
I've never seen real royalty before...

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.190
She really looks like a princess.

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.690
She has this aura about her.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.700
She's even more elegant than the celebrities at our school.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.030
I guess it's how she was raised...

00:11:25.030 --> 00:11:27.490
That's probably true, but...

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.080
She isn't like us commoners.

00:11:33.080 --> 00:11:36.050
Normally, she'd be far above us.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.710
I wonder if the cafeteria has emptied out yet.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.720
Fine, we'll take the back way.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.640
Right!

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:58.610
I see.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.900
I guess everyone's here to see the princess during lunch.

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:04.620
Wow. We're so far apart,

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.830
but she still looks wonderful!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.620
Seems like she's having fun.

00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:10.750
I'm glad.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.330
Now, let's go down and eat.

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:16.790
Everyone's so focused on the princess that the counter's open.

00:12:21.130 --> 00:12:24.130
Kato Marika, from the first-year high school snow class.

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.550
Please come to the high school nurse's office immediately.

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.520
Will take-out work?

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:32.350
Yeah.

00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.400
Thanks!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.110
Got it!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.440
<b>Treatment in progress.
No entry except
emergencies.</b>

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:44.660
That was smart.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.120
They say the best place to hide a tree would be in the forest.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:50.160
But if you announce where you're hiding her,

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.250
you limit what your enemy can do.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:54.120
I guess it was smart,

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.290
but everything that happened after was too sudden.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.130
I didn't know you could even make uniforms that fast.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.250
Those are tailor-made, right?

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.170
It's a good thing.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:04.010
Everyone worked to respond

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.970
to the captain's quick decision as fast as they could.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.510
So, what'd you want to talk about?

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.020
A special document.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:12.930
A special document?

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:15.940
It arrived for the Sea of the Morningstar Government,

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:17.940
from the Serenity Royal Government via an underground route.

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:20.150
When?

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.900
I thought you'd ask that...

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:25.200
Here.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.070
The comm logs say it was

00:13:27.070 --> 00:13:31.830
after your return to Sea of the Morningstar yesterday.

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.460
After we contacted the Insurance Union?

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:35.370
That's right.

00:13:35.370 --> 00:13:38.170
Quick to decide, quick to act.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.670
Unexpected, but not bad at all, huh?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:44.880
But isn't Serenity's response a little too fast?

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.510
It's like, you know...

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:47.550
It smells like a rat.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:50.220
You mean, "It smells fishy."

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:57.310
Wait, you aren't going to say I should ask Gruier directly about this suspicious stuff, are you?

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:58.350
Is that it?

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.020
That's right.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:03.530
It's good that your brain's started thinking that far ahead.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:04.740
I'll give you a gold star.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.860
I'd rather have a gold star on my tests...

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.370
Not happening.

00:14:09.370 --> 00:14:10.700
Figures...

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.620
Of course...

00:14:16.370 --> 00:14:19.670
Gotta get results myself.

00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:21.840
Why are you talking to yourself?

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:25.760
I was just thinking I need to study more.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.630
How's it looking this week with the pirates?

00:14:29.930 --> 00:14:31.800
Nothing for a while.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.640
The princess is here.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.350
We've gotta escort her and watch out for her.

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:40.190
What's your impression of Her Highness?

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:42.900
It looks like things are really hard for her.

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:44.940
She has her position as princess.

00:14:44.940 --> 00:14:46.900
She can't ever look upset.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:49.700
She always has to be in control.

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.660
But...

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.250
She still smiles that way sometimes...

00:14:56.250 --> 00:14:57.540
Wanna invite her over?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.960
Sounds fun, doesn't it?

00:15:02.170 --> 00:15:03.290
W-We can't!

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:04.420
She's a princess!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.310
Weren't we supposed to not have any work until next week?

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.480
Sorry. It was sudden.

00:15:27.730 --> 00:15:29.900
It hasn't even been five days.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.910
It's inside the Tau system.

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:34.490
We'll be back by dinner.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:35.580
Where's Kane?

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:37.540
He's your homeroom teacher, isn't he?

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.580
I got the message after homeroom.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:41.580
There he is.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.880
We don't want them arriving before us.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:50.550
Hurry.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:52.550
You're the one who's late!

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.800
I almost got stopped by a problem!

00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:56.140
A problem?

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.230
Misa, don't drive like that!

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:05.440
This gate always takes too long to open.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.610
It'll take twenty minutes to the airport, even if we rush, huh?

00:16:11.610 --> 00:16:12.910
Excuse me.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:18.910
What is this?

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:20.750
Don't blame me.

00:16:20.750 --> 00:16:22.330
I sent the captain on ahead.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:25.130
And then, when I left the classroom, the princess demanded to come too.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:27.040
It's a sudden job, right?

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:30.880
You're going to investigate a suspicious ship in the Tau system.

00:16:30.880 --> 00:16:33.630
The job's from the escort fleet's high command.

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.090
Am I right?

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.010
Is it?

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.890
I had planned to discuss the job on the way there.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:42.980
But that's right.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:44.560
Let's hurry.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:46.190
We can discuss the details as we go.

00:16:48.070 --> 00:16:48.940
I'm going to floor it!

00:17:01.160 --> 00:17:02.700
Okay, see you there.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:05.250
Thanks.

00:17:06.630 --> 00:17:07.790
You two okay?

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:14.470
I didn't know driving to the airport could be so stressful...

00:17:14.470 --> 00:17:17.970
We shouldn't talk like that.

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.400
I was a fool.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:31.860
I'm sorry.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:33.030
That's not true.

00:17:33.030 --> 00:17:37.660
So, shall we discuss the details in the shuttle?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:39.490
Okay... Okay.

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:56.470
I'll go over the job from the escort fleet's HQ again.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:57.880
I'll skip the exact coordinates,

00:17:58.390 --> 00:17:59.850
but an unknown ship is

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:03.310
due to arrive right on the edge of the Tau system.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:05.350
They want us to see who it is.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:10.060
The princess says it's a military ship from the Serenity system.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.740
It's bringing information on the golden ghost ship from the royal palace.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.030
I see.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:19.910
Serenity isn't an enemy, nor are they expected to be hostile.

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.990
But if another military's ship enters

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:24.830
their territory on a mission, the escort fleet can't ignore it.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:29.500
Nor do they want to make a big deal out of it.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:31.710
So they turn to the pirates.

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.920
The problem is that what I'm seeing suggests more than one ship.

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:40.590
And that the ships are engaged in combat.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:43.510
In other words, there's a possibility that

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.810
the Bentenmaru will be caught up in a fight.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:49.350
A fight...

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:02.820
Really?

00:19:02.820 --> 00:19:05.040
It's the same way here?

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:08.540
The princess was explaining things to us.

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.040
You all seemed to be having fun though.

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.090
Except for one of you.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:14.880
I've been busy.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.760
Well? How much of an explanation did you get?

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:19.470
From what she said,

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:23.220
the princess didn't think there was enough data

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.810
to capture the golden ghost ship,

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.480
and she sent a message to the palace...

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:31.440
To the palace?! Directly?

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.820
Yes. I used a secret method,

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:36.440
passed down through the Serenity Royal Family.

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.440
A secret method?

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.700
Well, if you can board the Bentenmaru,

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:43.620
I guess you can do anything...

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.950
So, what did you request?

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.540
I asked them to bring me their records

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.790
on the golden ghost ship from the palace.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.880
Honestly, I should have brought them myself.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:58.210
I apologize for being so ill-prepared.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.720
Well, it's actually considerate!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.640
Isn't it, Gruier?

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:05.970
Um...

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.930
That captain's outfit is very nice.

00:20:10.730 --> 00:20:11.390
This?

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:13.560
Yes! It looks very good on you.

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.110
I'd like to wear it too...

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:18.820
Isn't that nice, Captain?

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.110
Right, right!

00:20:20.110 --> 00:20:21.450
Everyone, return to your stations.

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:24.360
Get going. Hurry!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:34.830
The wind is harsher than usual...

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.210
They're nearly here.

00:20:37.210 --> 00:20:39.050
Bentenmaru, battle stations!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:45.010
You're worried about the ship, aren't you?

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:49.310
Probably because you heard they'll appear while engaged in combat, right?

00:20:49.310 --> 00:20:52.930
I believe in Serenity.

00:20:52.930 --> 00:20:55.270
Believe in her too.

00:21:02.320 --> 00:21:03.650
Here they are.

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:07.120
Detecting minor fluctuations off our bow.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:07.660
They're coming.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.330
A powerful military-class ship is touching down...

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:11.450
Pattern match!

00:21:11.450 --> 00:21:15.120
It's one of those Corbacks from the Serenity Defense Fleet.

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:21.510
Wait a second...

00:21:21.510 --> 00:21:23.130
It's putting out a lot of energy.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:25.010
It's damaged?

00:21:25.010 --> 00:21:26.050
Radar waves detected!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:30.060
So, it is in battle.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:32.640
Multiple fluctuations detected in the surrounding area.

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:35.770
What?

00:21:35.770 --> 00:21:39.110
What is the Serenity ship fighting?!

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.570
We'll know in a second.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:42.820
Multiple military-class ships!

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:50.370
Where are they from?

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:54.080
Identification complete. They're all Serenity Defense Forces.

00:21:54.080 --> 00:21:56.250
One battleship, four escorts.

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.330
Why?

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:59.460
Captain! Your orders?

00:22:06.130 --> 00:22:08.300
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.300 --> 00:22:10.930
The Princess and the Pirate

00:22:10.930 --> 00:22:12.510
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:18.020
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:18.020 --> 00:22:21.020
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:24.400
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.490
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:30.530
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:39.460
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.460 --> 00:22:44.340
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.630 --> 00:22:48.170
How far?

00:22:48.170 --> 00:22:50.840
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.840 --> 00:22:54.470
Until the end.

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:55.810
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:59.140
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:07.990
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.740
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:13.160
What should we do?

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:16.330
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:20.620
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:26.670
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:30.930
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:39.230 --> 00:23:41.020
Multiple factions within the royal palace.

00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:43.690
As the princess struggles against them alone,

00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:45.650
the girl offers her hand.

00:23:46.270 --> 00:23:49.320
What is the golden ghost ship that holds the key to ending the struggle?

00:23:50.150 --> 00:23:53.070
Destiny leads the girl into wider seas.

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:55.830
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.830 --> 00:23:57.160
A beautiful launch.

00:23:57.870 --> 00:23:59.000
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.000 --> 00:24:05.000
A Beautiful Launch

00:24:05.000 --> 00:24:10.510
Captain! Your orders?
